WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.621
Critical thinking is not only an individual skill.

00:00:02.621 --> 00:00:04.511
It is also a communication practice.

00:00:04.511 --> 00:00:08.607
Reasoning improves when people can explain what they believe, why they believe it,

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:11.128
what evidence supports it, and what uncertainty remains.

00:00:11.128 --> 00:00:12.703
Clear communication makes thinking reviewable.

00:00:12.703 --> 00:00:15.539
Vague confidence makes it hard for others to help.

00:00:15.539 --> 00:00:17.429
Good disagreement separates people from ideas.

00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:21.840
Challenging a claim is not the same as attacking the person who made it.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.991
In a healthy review, people ask clarifying questions, test assumptions,

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.882
and examine evidence while preserving respect.

00:00:26.882 --> 00:00:30.662
This matters because many errors survive not because no one noticed them,

00:00:30.662 --> 00:00:34.128
but because no one felt able to raise the concern clearly.

00:00:34.128 --> 00:00:37.909
Steelmanning is the practice of representing an opposing view in its strongest

00:00:37.909 --> 00:00:39.800
reasonable form before responding to it.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.005
This prevents weak rebuttals and performative certainty.

00:00:42.005 --> 00:00:45.156
If you can explain the strongest version of another view,

00:00:45.156 --> 00:00:47.992
you are more likely to understand the actual disagreement.

00:00:47.992 --> 00:00:52.088
Sometimes the exercise reveals that the opposing view has a point worth integrating.

00:00:52.088 --> 00:00:56.184
Peer review and decision review work best when assumptions and evidence are documented.

00:00:56.184 --> 00:00:59.965
A reviewer should not have to guess why a conclusion was reached.

00:00:59.965 --> 00:01:01.540
Decision records, brief evidence summaries,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.061
and explicit uncertainty help others assess the reasoning.

00:01:04.061 --> 00:01:08.157
They also make it easier to revisit a decision later when conditions change.

00:01:08.157 --> 00:01:12.253
Changing your mind when the evidence changes is a strength, not a failure.

00:01:12.253 --> 00:01:16.349
Performative certainty can feel impressive in the moment, but it makes teams brittle.

00:01:16.349 --> 00:01:19.184
Strong critical thinkers communicate confidence proportionally, invite useful challenge,

00:01:19.184 --> 00:01:22.020
and update their conclusions when the evidence justifies it.
